{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For</b> — here he showed that the multitude of the captives [were given] to chastisement because of their sins." "<b>And the word</b> המרו — or מרו is close in meaning." "<b>Thus they spurned</b> — from the light [root]. Or נאץ / ניאץ is the heavy [form]." "<b>And the sayings of</b> — to them the commandments of the heart, which HaShem planted in the heart of every speaker."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 107, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra distinguishes the qal (light) from the piel (heavy) binyan of the root נאץ."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:38:57.826522174Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}